    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nUsing the standard algorithm, we can calculate the sum of two numbers containing any number of digits.\n\nContent:\nLet's use the standard algorithm to compute the following sum:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 32,810+8,921]\n\nContent:\nThe procedure is the same as the one we've seen before. We start by lining up our numbers:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 3|2|8|1|0; +|8|9|2|1]\n\nContent:\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1|1; 3|2|8|1|0; +|8|9|2|1; 4|1|7|3|1]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: 32,810+8,921 = 41,731.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Five Digits\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 23,861+5,026?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 2|3|8|6|1; +|5|0|2|6]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 2|3|8|6|1; +|5|0|2|6; 2|8|8|8|7]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 23,861+5,026 = 28,887.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 23, 846 + 4, 123 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 29, 796]\nb. [MATH: 27, 969]\nc. [MATH: 29, 697]\nd. [MATH: 27, 996]\ne. [MATH: 26, 979]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 1, 241 + 4, 217 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5, 448]\nb. [MATH: 5, 458]\nc. [MATH: 5, 447]\nd. [MATH: 5, 455]\ne. [MATH: 5, 558]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Five Digits With Carrying\n\nExample Prompt:\nCompute the value of [MATH: 89,743+32,876.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 8|9|7|4|3; +|3|2|8|7|6]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 1|1|1|1; 8|9|7|4|3; +|3|2|8|7|6; 1|2|2|6|1|9]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 89,723+32,876 = 122,619.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 20, 129 + 9, 028 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 29, 157]\nb. [MATH: 28, 157]\nc. [MATH: 29, 257]\nd. [MATH: 29, 267]\ne. [MATH: 28, 167]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 42, 732 + 6, 598 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 48, 230]\nb. [MATH: 48, 030]\nc. [MATH: 49, 331]\nd. [MATH: 49, 330]\ne. [MATH: 48, 329]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Adding Numbers Up to Five Digits: Word Problems\n\nExample Prompt:\nMike wrote two essays. There are [MATH: 11,391] words in the first essay and [MATH: 7,942] words in the second essay. How many words did Mike write altogether?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find how many words Mike wrote altogether, we need to calculate the value of\n\n[MATH: 11,391 + 7,942.]\n\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 1|1|3|9|1; +|7|9|4|2]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers in each place value (from right to left):\n\n[MATH: 1|1; 1|1|3|9|1; +|7|9|4|2; 1|9|3|3|3]\n\nSo, [MATH: 11,391 + 7,942 = 19,333.]\n\nTherefore, Mike wrote [MATH: 19,333] words in total.\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nA household used [MATH: 14, 340] liters of water during September and [MATH: 9, 875] liters in October. How many liters of water did the household use during these two months?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 14, 215] liters\nb. [MATH: 23, 215] liters\nc. [MATH: 24, 115] liters\nd. [MATH: 24, 215] liters\ne. [MATH: 23, 115] liters\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nA supermarket sold [MATH: 91, 157] red apples and [MATH: 72, 865] green apples in July. How many apples did the supermarket sell in total?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 163, 022]\nb. [MATH: 94, 022]\nc. [MATH: 164, 022]\nd. [MATH: 164, 912]\ne. [MATH: 164, 812]"
